Well, yeah, but I'm afraid it's the only distinction that makes sense.
Magic Resistance reduces damage from:
* Magic missiles and magic missile breath.
* Artifact blasts
* Magical explosions (including snapped wands and exploding runes)
All of the above involve mana energy damage.

Meanwhile, Spell Resistance blocks the following:
* Death spell
* Polymorph spell (trap, wand and potion)
* Teleport spell (trap and wand)
* Force bolt spell
* Magicbane's magic absorption spell
* Monster spells (including curse objects, destroy armor et al)

I don't see any logical reason to move any of the members of column B
into column A.



